00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.640 line:92%
as opposed to a field of hate.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that is a difference
between you.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:12.679
A similarity is neither of you
have ever held political office.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
And obviously, there is some
hesitation by many voters

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that is an important thin
that you lack.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.120 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What do you say to them?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the question
is legitimate,

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:25.191 size:84% position:42%
but I think my answer
is significant as well.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all,
the problem with the President

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
is not that he lacked
experience.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
The problem with the President
is that he lacks ethics.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he seems to lack
a visceral taste for democracy

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
He lacks a visceral respec
for our democratic traditions.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:39.806 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I do not.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.975 size:88% position:44%
Now, as far as political
experience is concerned,

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he could have
surrounded himself

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.678
with very fine political experts
had he chosen to.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.050
Now, when you -- I have a lot of
respect for political expertise,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:50.850 line:92%
but let's not kid ourselves.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.654
Very experienced politicians
led us into the war in Iraq.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:59.459
Very experienced politicians
led us into the war in Vietnam

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.261 line:92%
We need political vision now

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much as we need
political expertise.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
You could have the best
car mechanic in the world,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.368
but the best car mechanic
doesn't necessarily know

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
what road you should take
to San Antonio.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.672 line:92%
That's what I feel I bring

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
And FDR said that
the primary responsibility

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the primary role
of the presidency, he said

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
is not the administrative
aspect.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.082 line:92%
That, he said, is secondary.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
The primary role
is moral leadership.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.219 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That is what we lack.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
We lack a vision of
where America is

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a vision of
where America needs to go.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that takes more than
political expertise,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I believe that
the experience I do have

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.665
and the skill set I do hav
makes me the woman for that job.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:42.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
